Feature: Lease teardown with guest sessions and remote sessions

  @AC-12 @TL-2 @TL-4
  Scenario: Release cancels a command running over a guest session
    Given a running lease on guest link "ssh-session"
    And an exec of "sleep 600" running
    When the orchestrator releases the lease
    Then the exec fails with "command cancelled by release"
    And no "sleep 600" process remains in the guest or on the host

  @AC-13 @TL-2 @TL-4
  Scenario: Release and destroy leave no guest session behind
    Given a lease with an open guest session
    When the orchestrator releases the lease
    Then the session's channel process has exited
    And no guest session agent process remains for that lease

  @AC-14 @TL-2
  Scenario: A daemon restart makes in-flight calls uncertain, never repeated
    Given a client with a remote session and an exec in flight
    When vm-service restarts
    Then the client's resume is answered "expired"
    And a query of the exec's execution ID answers "unknown"
    And the client reports the exec as uncertain without sending it again
